# Cursor Studio Project Planning

Relevant docs:
- Cursor rules and AGENTS.md: https://cursor.sh/docs/rules
- Cursor skills: https://cursor.sh/docs/skills
- Cursor commands and skills workflow: https://cursor.com/docs/agent/chat/commands
- VCU Supabase project/task rule: `.cursor/rules/vcu-supabase-project-tasks.mdc`

## Trigger Scenarios

Apply when turning verified VCU knowledge into project plans, task queues, assignment instructions, Cursor Studio plans, or Rust coding-agent work packets.

## Required Controls

- Start from accepted or explicitly review-stage source material; never invent task readiness.
- Include objective, source docs, target files/systems, required commands, expected outputs, and no-mock acceptance checks.
- Mark missing install/test/link/RLS evidence as `blocked` or `unverified`.
- Keep planning outputs separate from per-lesson artifacts unless the user requests lesson generation.

## May Change

- Project plans, task assignment drafts, operating-layer prompts, and reports.

## May Not Change

- Supabase task status, project completion status, or agent execution evidence without real verification.

## Verifiable Output

Return task plan IDs or draft names, source URLs, acceptance checks, command requirements, and every unverified dependency.
